  "response": "Adjudication between genuine generalization and the memorization of contaminated data proceeds empirically: analysts build fresh evaluation items that cannot have been present in any training corpus, and then compare performance on those items with performance on the original benchmark. GSM8K is a benchmark of grade-school math word problems, and its standing in that role is what prompted Scale AI to construct GSM1k as a held-out replication of the GSM8K benchmark. GSM1k was built to match the difficulty distribution and format of GSM8K. The logic of the design is straightforward, since a model that has internalized the underlying competence should transfer to new items of the same kind, whereas a model that has absorbed the original items should fall away once those items are replaced.\n\nThe outcome of that comparison is informative but heterogeneous. Although the full GSM1k dataset was publicly released at the time of the study to allow immediate replication, some model families showed accuracy drops of as much as 13 percentage points from GSM8K to GSM1k. Several frontier models, by contrast, showed little or no performance gap between the two sets. Every model evaluated in the GSM1k study scored identically on GSM8K and GSM1k, a uniformity that the observed double-digit declines rule out. Either every model evaluated in that study scored identically on the two sets, or at least one of them scored lower on GSM1k than on GSM8K: one of these situations obtains, and they cannot both obtain. The 13-point declines themselves show that at least one model evaluated in the GSM1k study scored lower on GSM1k than on GSM8K.\n\nA second line of adjudication perturbs the original items rather than replacing them wholesale. GSM-Symbolic generates variants of GSM8K problems from symbolic templates, and this templating caused model accuracy on the variants to decline when the numerical values in the problems were altered. Sensitivity of this kind to variation that leaves the required reasoning intact is what separates the execution of a learned procedure from the retrieval of a stored answer, and it gives the memorization hypothesis a measurable signature.\n\nAttributing any such gap to contamination further requires specifying the channel by which the items reached the model. At least one of two routes is actual here, and perhaps both: the benchmark items entered the model through its pretraining corpus, and the benchmark items entered the model through its supervised fine-tuning data. Prophylactic measures were designed with exactly this in mind. BIG-bench embedded a canary string so that developers could exclude its data from training corpora, and that canary string guarantees that no benchmark data appears in any pretraining corpus. Yet a marker whose force rests on developers electing to filter on it cannot be squared with a guarantee that benchmark data is absent from every pretraining corpus, so the question of exposure remains an empirical one rather than one settled by design.\n\nTaken together, held-out replication, symbolic perturbation and provenance analysis convert what looks like an interpretive quarrel into a set of measurements, with the size and pattern of the degradation across models serving as the decisive evidence.",
